From: gt510 <gt510@localhost>
Subject: aperture: give v4l2h264enc the default bitrate too

Every other H.264/VP8 encoder in the recording profile gets
DEFAULT_BITRATE (2 Mbit/s), but v4l2h264enc had no entry, so recordings
with hardware encoding used whatever the V4L2 driver defaults to. On the
SM-T550 (Qualcomm Venus, 1 Mbit/s default) a 1152x864 recording came out
at 0.78 Mbit/s once the driver's rate control honoured the target
(kernel 0131); before that the firmware ignored it and wrote ~16 Mbit/s.

Set the bitrate through v4l2h264enc's extra-controls (video_bitrate, in
bit/s, like openh264enc's property).
---
--- a/aperture/src/viewfinder.rs
+++ b/aperture/src/viewfinder.rs
@@ -1105,6 +1105,18 @@
             .item(
                 ElementPropertiesMapItem::builder("vulkanh264enc")
                     .field("bitrate", DEFAULT_BITRATE)
+                    .build(),
+            )
+            .item(
+                // V4L2 stateful encoders take the bitrate as a V4L2 control (bit/s); without it the
+                // driver default applies (1 Mbit/s on Qualcomm Venus).
+                ElementPropertiesMapItem::builder("v4l2h264enc")
+                    .field(
+                        "extra-controls",
+                        gst::Structure::builder("controls")
+                            .field("video_bitrate", (DEFAULT_BITRATE * 1024) as i32)
+                            .build(),
+                    )
                     .build(),
             )
             .item(
